From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: a DrawAuto in a capturing draw pauses the capture first

A DrawAuto (glDrawTransformFeedback) ends the capture that wrote its vertex buffer, binding that capture's transform
feedback object for the End. The draw's own capture is begun or resumed before that, and GL binds no other object
while a capture runs unpaused: the bind failed, the End ended the draw's own capture, and the source stayed active.
Stream output ping-ponged between two buffers with DrawAuto (3DMark Vantage's GPU cloth and particles) then failed
every later Begin (GL_INVALID_OPERATION) and lost the context. The running capture is now paused around the bind and
resumed after.
---
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -5983,9 +5983,15 @@
       return false;
 
    if (found->xfb_state == XFB_STATE_PAUSED || found->xfb_state == XFB_STATE_STARTED) {
+      /* the draw's own capture already runs: GL binds no other object while it isn't paused (the End then ends it) */
+      bool resume = sub_ctx->current_so && sub_ctx->current_so->xfb_state == XFB_STATE_STARTED;
+      if (resume)
+         glPauseTransformFeedback();
       glBindTransformFeedback(GL_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK, found->id);
       glEndTransformFeedback();
       glBindTransformFeedback(GL_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK, sub_ctx->current_so ? sub_ctx->current_so->id : 0);
+      if (resume)
+         glResumeTransformFeedback();
       found->xfb_state = XFB_STATE_STARTED_NEED_BEGIN;
       found->ended = true;
    }
